# eephus.io betting + card jobs. Install on the production box with `crontab -e`.
#
# Three jobs, and only one of them costs API credits (the card job spends only
# marketplace requests, throttled to one per 5s).
#
# TZ=UTC BELOW IS LOAD-BEARING, AND ITS ABSENCE IS THE PRIME SUSPECT FOR THE
# ZERO CLOSE SNAPSHOTS (2026-08-09 owner decision, binding). This file used to
# ship the close job as `*/15 12-23 * * *` in the BOX's local clock and tell the
# reader to confirm the box timezone by hand. Nobody did, the box timezone is
# undocumented, and if the box runs UTC that window is 08:00 to 19:00 Eastern:
# it shuts before a 7:05pm ET first pitch on most of the calendar and misses
# every late slate outright. Measured on 2026-08-09 the odds cache held 4 open
# snapshots and ZERO close snapshots, so CLV had never been gradeable for any
# slate, and CLV is unrecoverable after the fact.
#
# The fix is not a better window. It is NO window: the job now runs every 15
# minutes all day and `decide()` does every piece of clock reasoning against UTC
# instants read off the schedule. That is correct under any box timezone. TZ=UTC
# is set anyway so the log stamps and the job's own reasoning agree, and so a
# reader of `crontab -l` can see which clock these lines are in.
#
# THE ENVIRONMENT IS THE PART PEOPLE GET WRONG. cron runs with almost no
# environment: no PATH beyond /usr/bin:/bin, no shell profile, no virtualenv.
# The API key must be visible to the job or every run is a silent no-op that
# looks healthy in the log. Either set it here (this file is not in git, but
# `crontab -l` shows it to anyone on the box) or, better, keep it in a
# root-owned EnvironmentFile and source it in the wrapper.

SHELL=/bin/bash
TZ=UTC                                         # <- every line below is UTC
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
EEPHUS=/opt/eephus/prospect-tracker           # <- the checkout on this box
PY=/opt/eephus/venv/bin/python                 # <- the interpreter with the deps

# --- The close odds snapshot, for closing line value ------------------------
# Runs every 15 minutes, ALL DAY, and DECIDES each time. It exits quietly on
# every invocation except the one inside the window (10 minutes before the
# slate's earliest first pitch), so no cron window is needed and doubleheaders,
# rain delays, schedule changes and a 10:10pm ET first pitch all handle
# themselves.
#
# 96 invocations a day sounds expensive and costs nothing: `decide()` reads
# artifacts, spends no credit, and the job refuses to fire twice for the same
# slate date. The guard is a real lookup of today's close snapshot, not a
# lockfile, so it holds across reboots. Spend stays 3 credits a day, once, out
# of 500 a month.
#
# Check what it is doing without spending anything:
#   $PY tools/betting_close_job.py --why
#
# AND AFTER INSTALLING, RUN THIS, because --why does not answer the question
# that was actually wrong for months:
#   $PY tools/betting_close_job.py --selfcheck
# --why says what the job WOULD do now, which reads the same on a box where
# nothing is scheduled. --selfcheck says whether the SCHEDULER has ever reached
# the job on this machine, by reading the heartbeat the job stamps on every
# invocation including its refusals. Exit 1 and "NEVER RUN on this machine"
# means this crontab entry is not installed or not firing; fix that before
# concluding anything else about the betting module.
*/15 * * * *  cd $EEPHUS && . /etc/eephus.env && $PY tools/betting_close_job.py >> logs/betting-close.log 2>&1

# --- The leaderboard vintage snapshot, the validation clock -----------------
# Offline, idempotent, about 25KB a night, costs no credits. This is the ONLY
# thing that can ever make the betting backtest honest, and a missed night is
# missed permanently: nothing in the tree can reconstruct what the leaderboards
# said on a past date. The nightly pipeline already calls it at step 9e-pre;
# this belt-and-braces entry covers the nights the pipeline does not run.
# Idempotent by design (first write wins), so running both is harmless.
17 6 * * *  cd $EEPHUS && $PY leaderboard_vintages.py --snapshot >> logs/vintage.log 2>&1

# --- Checks you can run by hand --------------------------------------------
#   $PY tools/betting_close_job.py --why      today's window, spends nothing
#   $PY -c "import betting_export as be, json; print(json.dumps(
#            be.snapshot_health(14), indent=1, default=str))"
#                                             per-slate open/close coverage off
#                                             .cache/odds/, hours since the last
#                                             close, and a diagnosis that names
#                                             the REPAIR. Read this before
#                                             concluding the close job works: the
#                                             capture, not the exit code, is the
#                                             evidence, and the job exits 0 on
#                                             every legitimate no-op.
#   $PY betting_ingest.py --status            is a key configured (never prints it)
#   $PY leaderboard_vintages.py --coverage    how many vintages exist
#
# /etc/eephus.env should be root-owned, chmod 600, and contain:
#   export EEPHUS_ODDS_API_KEY=...
